{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For Sheol does not thank you.</b> The meaning concerns the body buried in Sheol; [the word לא draws itself and another along with it], and likewise מות לא יהללך, like מתן בסתר יכפה אף (Proverbs 21:14):" "<b>They will pine.</b> Like ייחלו, like עיני כל אליך ישברו (Psalms 145:15). Many wonder how the prophet wrote words such as these, which deny the resurrection of the dead. One may answer that the body has no power and no knowledge when the soul departs from it — and why should they wonder, when even while the soul is joined to the body it does not understand, all the more so in its death:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The bracketed grammatical remark is obscure in the original; rendered literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:56.390081741Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}